  "answer_text": "Depending on the context, you are likely referring to one of the following notable people:\n\n### 1. **Katherine McCoy** (often spelled or searched as *Catherine McCoy*)\nShe is a highly influential and pioneering **American graphic designer and design educator**. \n* **Career & Cranbrook:** She is best known for her landmark tenure as the co-chair of the graduate Design department at the **Cranbrook Academy of Art** (alongside her husband, Michael McCoy) from 1971 to 1995. Under her leadership, Cranbrook became a hotbed for experimental and revolutionary graphic design. \n* **Design Philosophy:** McCoy is famous for integrating post-structuralist literary theory, semiotics, and \"deconstruction\" into graphic design, urging designers to think of their work as \"text\" to be read, rather than just images to be looked at.\n* **Awards:** She was awarded the prestigious **AIGA Medal** in 1999 for her immense contributions to design education and practice.\n\n---\n\n### 2. **Catherine McCoy** (Naturopath & Author)\nIf you are looking for someone in the health and wellness space, Catherine McCoy is a well-known **Australian integrative naturopath, herbalist, and health coach**.\n* She is the founder of the **iNaturally Clinic** in Canberra, Australia. \n* She has over two decades of experience in clinical practice, focusing largely on helping women manage fatigue, stress, and hormonal burnout. \n* She is also an author, known for creating the *Rebuild Your Life Journal* and *The Fatigue Solution*.",
